File 4: charts/addons/locals.tf — only if Kyverno blocks your ECR image

Your repo has an image registry restriction allow-list.

Current area:

image_registry_restriction_allow_list = try(var.addon_config.image_registry_restriction_allow_list, "...")

If your cluster has this policy enforced, and your new ECR image repo is not already included, the Superset pod may be denied.

What to do

Check whether your ECR registry path is already allowed.

If not, add your ECR image pattern into that allow-list string.

Example

If your image is:

123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/my-superset:6.0.0-custom

hen add something like:

| 123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/my-superset:*

inside the allow-list string.

Example modified snippet
image_registry_restriction_allow_list = try(
  var.addon_config.image_registry_restriction_allow_list,
  "602401143452.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/amazon-k8s-cni:* | ... | us-docker.pkg.dev/fairwinds-ops/oss/goldilocks:* | 123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/my-superset:*"
)

Only do this if your admission policy blocks the image.
